CommitDate: Sat Sep 19 14:12:53 2026 -0500

    fix(installer): DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-22 — prefix-scope rule packs skip instead of installing inert
    
    With a custom TERMINAL_JAIL_INSTALL_DIR and no rules-dir override, the
    installer resolved <prefix>/config/terminal-jail/rules.d and --rule-pack
    byte-copied the pack there with a success line and exit 0 — but the engine
    loads only /etc/terminal-jail/rules.d and ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d
    (or TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_RULES_DIR / TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR),
    so the pack was silently inert and psql destructive-command rules never fired.
    
    Two changes, preserving the default install, same-id precedence, the DF-21
    skip contract, and the engine's documented rules-directory contract:
    
    - New resolver case (engine-env): with a custom prefix and an exported
      TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR (the engine's own user-rules
      variable, read verbatim at run time), the installer's single rules dir
      resolves to exactly that directory — default rules AND packs land where
      the engine actually loads. An explicit TERMINAL_JAIL_RULES_DIR still wins.
    - Remaining prefix-local scope: every requested pack is SKIPPED before the
      validator runs — one stderr reason naming the inert target and the exact
      remediation (explicit TERMINAL_JAIL_RULES_DIR; TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR
      exported for BOTH install and run; or the default install dir) — under the
      DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-21 contract: nothing written for the pack, base install
      always completes, end summary + exit 2. --unrule-pack is removal and stays
      available in every scope. The prefix default-rules WARNING now also names
      the engine-env channel and the pack skip.
    
    Tests: new DF-22 regressions pin the prefix skip (exit 2, remediation named,
    no pack file, base install completes; two packs skip independently) and the
    engine-loaded channels (pack byte-copied to the explicit / engine-env
    directory and intercept() BLOCKs the DROP DATABASE vector through it — a
    load proof, not a file-presence proof). The engine-loaded pack tests
    (validation refusals, PyYAML/JSON/no-python3 preflights, collision oracle)
    moved to the explicit-rules-dir scope, where an installed pack is really
    loaded. RED-proven: the new prefix test fails against 808ff39's install.sh
    (silent exit 0) and passes with the fix.
    
    Docs: README, docs/quickstart.md, specs/cli.md, CHANGELOG.md updated to
    document the engine-env channel, the prefix pack skip, and the remediation.
    
    Gates: pytest 889 passed / 5 skipped (unchanged skips), uvx ruff check clean,
    scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py ALL PROBES PASS (byte-identical mirror).
    
    Addresses DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-22.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
